ADDITIONAL TERM under section 7(b) of the GNU GPL version 3
-----------------------------------------------------------

As permitted by section 7(b), the following additional term applies to the
GPL-3.0-or-later portions of PiVid, and may not be removed:

    You must preserve the author attribution

        PiVid - Copyright (C) 2026 Pi - https://github.com/NotAPastry/pivid

    in the Appropriate Legal Notices displayed by works containing this
    software. Where the work presents a user interface, an "About" screen, a
    version banner, or equivalent, the attribution must appear there. In
    PiVid's own binaries this attribution is carried in the pivid-config-agent
    web interface and in the --version output; a modified version must not
    remove or obscure it.

This term requires only the preservation of an existing attribution. It does
not require attribution in advertising, and it does not restrict any freedom
granted by the GPL. Under section 7 you may remove this term only from
material you did not receive under it.


================================================================================
2. KERNEL CODE — GNU General Public License v2.0 only  (GPL-2.0-only)
================================================================================

    drivers/lr2021/
    patches/bcm2835-codec-controls.patch
    patches/bcm2835-codec-intra-refresh-slices.patch
    patches/bcm2835-codec-resilience-phase2.patch
    tests/driver/
    tests/integration/test_frame_sync_fec.c

These are derivative works of the Linux kernel, which is GPL-2.0-only, and
therefore cannot be relicensed. The lr2021 driver already declares
MODULE_LICENSE("GPL"). The listed test files #include headers from
drivers/lr2021/ and inherit that licence.

The GPL-2.0-only driver and the GPL-3.0-or-later userspace are separate
programs. They communicate only across the kernel/userspace boundary via the
character device and ioctl interface in common/radio_ioctl.h; they are not
linked together, and no combined work is formed.

Full text: LICENSES/GPL-2.0-only.txt


================================================================================
3. UAPI BOUNDARY — GNU General Public License v2.0 or later  (GPL-2.0-or-later)
================================================================================

    common/radio_ioctl.h

This header defines the kernel/userspace ABI and is included from both sides.
It is licensed v2-or-later so that the GPL-2.0-only driver and the
GPL-3.0-or-later userspace may each include it without conflict.


